turnip: darwin, cached and freed BOs go back when idle; every GPU process gives its cache back when a BoAlloc finds no memory

Every BO piano's kernel gives (PianoA830) is wired memory of the system. On the first macOS desktop sessions (2026-11-12, image
desk-dev) XNU had no pages left to wire: WindowServer's BoAllocs failed (`gpu BoAlloc refused: 49 MiB: pool 168 MiB free, largest
19; then no pages from XNU (0xe00002bd NoMemory)`), its textures were refused with OutOfMemory(Device) and SkyLight aborted, twice in
five minutes. Nineteen GPU processes held GPU memory then, and none of them was under the memory pressure the frameworks purge on
(memory_pressure: 22 % free): what each had cached or freed stayed. On the native darwin path:
- A cached BO no allocation took within TU_DARWIN_BO_CACHE_AGE_MS (2000 by default; 0: kept for good, as before) goes back to the
  kernel: at the next allocation, and by a one-shot dispatch timer (on a serial queue of the device's own) armed only while something
  is cached or a freed BO waits for its fence, with a leeway of half the age (at most a second) so the system can coalesce its
  wake-up. An idle process with nothing cached is never woken. The same timer reaps the freed BOs whose fence passed while the process
  did nothing else (they waited for its next allocation or free before). The device's finish stops the timer (out of the device
  list, cancelled, a running handler waited for) before the connection closes.
- The cache budgets follow the connection's GPU window when TU_DARWIN_BO_CACHE_MB / TU_DARWIN_BO_CACHE_SMALL_MB are not set: the
  render server's (2 GiB or more, or the VM's virtio GPU) 96 and 16 MiB as before, a large client's (512 MiB or more) 32 and 8, a
  small one's 16 and 4.
- A BoAlloc that finds no memory (kIOReturnNoMemory) after this process's own cache went back posts the Darwin notification
  `org.unixnu.piano.gpu-reclaim` (at most every 50 ms per process): every GPU process registered for it (with the memory-pressure
  source) gives its whole cache back now, through its timer. The BoAlloc is tried again after 4, 8, 16, 32 and 64 ms, reaping this
  process's own freed BOs before each; once a whole series failed, none waits again for a second. On stderr, the first time and then
  every 10th, 100th, ...: "TU: error: NativeAdreno: a BoAlloc found no memory; every GPU process was asked for its cached BOs; made
  after N waits (K times)" or "... still none after 5 waits ...".
- The cache's log line (every 4096 lookups and at the device's end) has a third line: the BOs given back after the age, the idle
  trims, the reclaims asked and answered, the BoAlloc waits and how many made it.
Against the tree after 0001-0008. MIT, as the files.

